1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,632
In this workshop an open-top box is made from a square piece of cardboard twenty-four inches on a side.

2
00:00:06,582 --> 00:00:11,888
A square of side x is cut from each corner, and then the edges are folded up.

3
00:00:11,888 --> 00:00:18,138
If you cut a little, the box is very shallow, and if you cut a lot, the base gets smaller.

4
00:00:18,138 --> 00:00:25,332
Drag the orange sphere at the corner, move the slider or the point on the graph, and see how the volume changes.

5
00:00:25,332 --> 00:00:32,978
With Unfold you see the flat cardboard with the cuts, and with Fill with sand you can compare the volumes of different boxes.

6
00:00:32,978 --> 00:00:37,885
Finally, check your result with Go to optimum or with Reveal solution.

